n-\n-\n class MergedCurrentSummaryTest(unittest.TestCase):\n@@\n         self.assertEqual(data[\"backlog\"][\"open\"], 1)\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    unittest.main()\n```\n\n</details>","id":"c7b236d935ae91f57bd4017aa02ee2b3c3cbebe7cf353f599e2e9071e309fe16","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_status_summary.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Move the `unittest.main()` guard to the end of the file."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"3313cceb88037081e98fc526b9461c7129626747","body":"**Reconcile the repair model descriptions.**\n\n`apps/crq-python/README.md:158-163` describes a model switch during peak hours. The committed roles use GLM, and an enabled blackout blocks dispatch instead of switching models.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Update the repair policy</summary>\n\n```diff\n-A0 uses the window's fixer. A mechanical failure retries the same model at A1,\n+A0 uses the configured fixer. A mechanical failure retries the fixer at A1,\n then escalation at A2; three fixer attempts and one judge are the ceiling.\n-Provider rate limits defer without consuming an attempt. The job's window stays\n-pinned across attempts. Weekday 14:00–18:00 Asia/Singapore uses Luna fixers and\n-Muse judges; default workers/judges use GLM Flash (D9 configurable). Critical\n-judgements use Sol in both windows. Recurring NOT-FIXED majors and configured\n+Provider rate limits defer without consuming an attempt. The configured models\n+are listed in Runtime ownership above. Recurring NOT-FIXED majors and configured\n sampling trigger a read-only judge; valid findings receive one A2 refix.\n```\n\n</details>","id":"d9aba1ed2200e0c8bc236f3a615c839be9792de5f4a9c366c6a39a8293c57453","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/README.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reconcile the repair model descriptions."}],"head":"e9afd3be83508ca8f7318751622569700d1bb02a","head_tree":"b4ccd79a879cd59b7eca92377c3b119eff95db28",